==Northern Sami==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|se|leahkit}}

===Etymology===
{{rfe|lang=se}}
Cognate with Pite Sami {{m|sje|årrot}} (most forms except the infinitive), Lule Sami {{m|smj|liehket}}, Skolt Sami {{m|sms|leeˊd}}, Inari Sami {{m|smn|leđe}}.
Related to Proto-Finnic {{m|fiu-fin-pro|*leedäk}}, from which Finnish {{m|fi|lienee}}, the ([[suppletive]]) potential form of {{m|fi|olla||to be}}.

===Verb===
{{se-verb}}

# to [[be]]
# {{lb|se|possessor in locative case}} to [[have]], to [[possess]]
# {{lb|se|auxiliary}} {{n-g|Forms the perfect tense, together with a past participle.}}

====Usage notes====
In the meaning "have", the thing possessed is in the nominative case, while the possessor is in the locative case.

